  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, the most critical need is to establish a reliable performance reference point for multimodal fusion using well-understood, standard components. config_005 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion) tests the core hypothesis—whether combining RNA and image modalities is viable—while keeping the design simple: pca_n2000 is the most standard and interpretable RNA encoder, imagenet_vit_l is a strong pretrained image encoder, weighted fusion is interpretable (revealing relative modality contribution), and singleprofile with no aggregation eliminates two sources of complexity. If this baseline performs well, it gives a target to beat and confirms the multimodal pipeline; if it underperforms, the failure is likely in the basic fusion or modality contribution rather than in complex aggregation or multiprofile handling. This maximizes the information gained per experiment under a limited budget by reducing confounding variables and establishing a clean anchor for all subsequent comparisons."
}

